    <p>For a writer who wants both tools on one computer, the cheapest lasting setup is the $150 Plottr lifetime plan plus one $59.99 Scrivener licence: $209.99 once. kindling adds nothing to that, and can stand in for either if the cost is the problem. The <a href="/blog/plottr-review/">Plottr review</a> covers which Plottr plan is worth it.</p>

    <h3>What the price buys</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Trials.</strong> Plottr has a 30-day free trial and no free plan. Scrivener’s trial lasts <a href="https://www.literatureandlatte.com/scrivener/faqs">30 days of actual use</a>, so opening it every other day stretches it to about two months. Scrivener for iOS has no trial.</li>
      <li><strong>When a Plottr plan ends.</strong> The standard Plottr app keeps working after a yearly plan lapses; it stops receiving updates. A lapsed Pro plan also loses access to your projects until you renew, because Pro keeps them in the cloud.</li>
      <li><strong>Scrivener upgrades.</strong> A licence covers one platform, and minor updates are free. Major versions, such as the move from Scrivener 1 to 3, have been paid upgrades.</li>
      <li><strong>Refunds.</strong> Plottr does not offer refunds. Instead it offers up to five hours of outlining coaching if the app doesn’t help you finish an outline.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

